<title>GERMANY: Gaddum sees agreement with Bonn on assets dispute.</title>
<headline>Gaddum sees agreement with Bonn on assets dispute.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank deputy president Johann Wilhelm Gaddum said on Friday that he was sure the central bank and Bonn government could reach an agreement over a government plan to revalue the central bank's assets.</p>
<p>&quot;I am firmly convinced that we can reach a satisfactory solution for both sides in the question of accounting methods,&quot; he said in a speech to a banking conference in Frankfurt.</p>
<p>He also said that the Bundesbank had stressed its own independence on monetary poicy in recent times. &quot;And that has been well recognised by the government,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
